WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.638
Changing the Constitution isn't one

2
00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:04.379
procedure. It's three,

3
00:00:04.379 --> 00:00:05.925
and the hardest one needs

4
00:00:05.925 --> 00:00:07.690
the states to agree.

5
00:00:08.018 --> 00:00:10.253
Some provisions change by a

6
00:00:10.253 --> 00:00:11.681
simple majority,

7
00:00:11.681 --> 00:00:13.989
and don't count as amendments

8
00:00:13.989 --> 00:00:15.758
under Article 368.

9
00:00:15.758 --> 00:00:17.666
Most need a special majority

10
00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:18.765
in each House.

11
00:00:18.765 --> 00:00:20.954
Federal provisions also need half

12
00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.958
the state legislatures.

13
00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.069
The election of the President

14
00:00:25.069 --> 00:00:26.404
needs the states.

15
00:00:26.404 --> 00:00:28.062
So do the Seventh Schedule's

16
00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:30.290
lists, and the states' representation

17
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.656
in Parliament.

18
00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:33.425
One more trap.

19
00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:34.864
For an amendment bill,

20
00:00:34.864 --> 00:00:36.411
there is no joint sitting

21
00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:38.327
if the Houses disagree.

22
00:00:39.018 --> 00:00:40.195
Your turn.

23
00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:42.015
What happens if the Houses

24
00:00:42.015 --> 00:00:43.154
disagree?
